---
/** Montgomery's two kinds of plumbing calls: lake homes and the historic town. */
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="lt-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="lt-h">On the lake, or in town?</h2>
    <div class="lt">
      <article>
        <h3>Lake homes</h3>
        <p>Weekend houses, docks, outdoor kitchens, attic water heaters and grinder pumps. Leaks run longer when nobody's home, so shut-offs and a routine matter.</p>
        <p><a href="/guides/lake-house-plumbing-checklist">Lake house plumbing checklist</a></p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Historic Montgomery and acreage</h3>
        <p>Older buildings around the historic district, newer homes on the edges of town, and acreage with wells and septic out toward Dobbin.</p>
        <p><a href="/areas/historic-downtown-montgomery">Historic downtown Montgomery</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lt { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .lt article { padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--bg-soft); }
  .lt article:first-child { border-left: 6px solid var(--accent); }
  .lt article:last-child { border-left: 6px solid #a3743a; }
  .lt p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 46rem) { .lt { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
</style>
